---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
import "../styles/system.css";
---

<Default
  title="posttrainllm — an open-source LLM factory that lives on your Mac"
  description="Distill routed specialists, package them for MLX, and know exactly where they fail. Train, fine-tune (LoRA / DoRA / QLoRA), evaluate (BFCL / τ-bench / lm-eval / SQL), serve OpenAI-compatible, and inspect with SAE / MEMIT / patching — all on one Apple Silicon machine. MIT. Built in the open by one developer."
  themeColor="#f5f6f8"
  ogTitle="posttrainllm — an open-source LLM factory that lives on your Mac"
  ogDescription="Distill, fine-tune, evaluate, serve, and inspect LLMs on a single Mac. Runs in a browser tab too. MIT."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="topbar" role="banner">
    <a class="brand-lockup" href="/" aria-label="posttrainllm home">
      <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">p</span>
      <span class="brand-name">posttrainllm</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="topnav" aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="/artifacts">specialists</a>
      <a href="/docs/attempt-ledger">experiments</a>
      <a href="/docs/learn/curriculum">learn</a>
      <a href="/leaderboard">evals</a>
      <a href="/playground">playground</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/sarthak-fleet/posttrainllm" rel="noopener">github ↗</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="landing" id="main">

    <!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <p class="hero-kicker mono-label">MIT · one developer · Apple Silicon</p>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">
        An LLM factory that fits<br />on <span class="ox">one&nbsp;Mac</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        posttrainllm turns a stock open model into a <em>routed specialist</em> that
        earns its keep — then tells you exactly where it fails. Distill, fine-tune,
        gate on real evals, package for MLX, and open the model up with
        interpretability. 100+ CLI subcommands, one Apple&nbsp;Silicon machine, no cloud.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/artifacts">See the specialists</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/quickstart">Read the quickstart</a>
      </div>

      <!-- live factory-loop specimen -->
      <figure class="loop" data-theme="instrument" aria-label="The factory loop">
        <figcaption class="loop-cap">
          <span class="mono-label">the loop the runtime closes</span>
          <span class="loop-live"><span class="dot"></span> last run 2026-07-11</span>
        </figcaption>
        <ol class="loop-steps" role="list">
          <li><span class="ls-n">01</span><span class="ls-k">target</span><code>frozen</code></li>
          <li><span class="ls-n">02</span><span class="ls-k">data</span><code>5,675 rows</code></li>
          <li><span class="ls-n">03</span><span class="ls-k">post-train</span><code>dpo · 200 steps</code></li>
          <li><span class="ls-n">04</span><span class="ls-k">eval</span><code class="ok">exec 0.920</code></li>
          <li><span class="ls-n">05</span><span class="ls-k">package</span><code>tgla / mlx</code></li>
          <li class="ls-decide"><span class="ls-n">06</span><span class="ls-k">decide</span><code>retry-data</code></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="loop-note">
          Every run assembles a schema-valid folder — config, dataset, eval, decision,
          report — that <code>factory-run</code> validates. The one proof still missing
          is a run whose decision is <span class="ship">ship</span>.
        </p>
      </figure>

      <ul class="hero-stats" role="list">
        <li><b>0.920</b><span>SQL execution, on-device</span></li>
        <li><b>100%</b><span>file-ops hard gate (from 58%)</span></li>
        <li><b>1×</b><span>Apple Silicon, zero cloud</span></li>
        <li><b>MIT</b><span>open, one developer</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= SPECIALISTS ================= -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <header class="band-head">
          <h2>Specialists that are honest by design.</h2>
          <p class="band-sub">
            A specialist beats a generalist on its target and routes away when it
            shouldn't answer. Every result here ships with the regression it costs.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="spec-grid">
          <article class="spec spec-lead">
            <div class="spec-top">
              <span class="mono-label">released · weights</span>
              <h3>Qwen3-4B, file-ops distilled</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="spec-body">
              Distilled to <strong>100%</strong> on the multi-turn file-ops hard gate
              (BFCL), up from 58%. The honest cost: out-of-domain breadth dropped
              <strong>60% → 42%</strong> — real catastrophic forgetting. So it ships
              <em>routed</em>, never as a general planner.
            </p>
            <dl class="spec-metrics">
              <div><dt>file-ops gate</dt><dd>58% → <b>100%</b></dd></div>
              <div><dt>OOD breadth</dt><dd class="down">60% → 42%</dd></div>
              <div><dt>size</dt><dd>4B · MLX</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="spec-link" href="/docs/learn/tool-calling-frontier-parity">The distillation write-up →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="spec">
            <div class="spec-top">
              <span class="mono-label">report-only candidate</span>
              <h3>Qwen3-0.6B, routed SQL</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="spec-body">
              Two adapters behind a router: public schema-SQL and local execution-SQL.
              Two reference-anchored DPO retries cured a policy collapse and pushed
              execution to <strong>0.920</strong> — but output hygiene is a base-model
              prior a small adapter can't strip. Decision: <em>retry-data</em>.
            </p>
            <dl class="spec-metrics">
              <div><dt>synthetic exec</dt><dd>0.860 → <b>0.920</b></dd></div>
              <div><dt>public exact</dt><dd>0.531</dd></div>
              <div><dt>clean-SQL</dt><dd class="down">0.000</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="spec-link" href="/artifacts/qwen06-sql-routed-v1">Full artifact + blockers →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
        <a class="band-more" href="/artifacts">Every artifact, with evidence and blockers →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= MEASURED ================= -->
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <header class="band-head">
          <h2>Measured, on one machine.</h2>
          <p class="band-sub">Every number below was recorded on a single M5&nbsp;Pro / 48&nbsp;GB. No estimates.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="metric-row" role="list">
          <div role="listitem"><b>76</b><span class="mu">tok/s</span><small>4B decode, MLX</small></div>
          <div role="listitem"><b>12.1×</b><span class="mu">speedup</span><small>WebGPU vs WASM, XL</small></div>
          <div role="listitem"><b>&lt;45s</b><span class="mu">per pass</span><small>50-row SQL eval</small></div>
          <div role="listitem"><b>0</b><span class="mu">spikes</span><small>200k pretrain steps</small></div>
          <div role="listitem"><b>2×</b><span class="mu">half memory</span><small>ref-free vs DPO</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= WHAT SHIPS ================= -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <header class="band-head">
          <h2>The whole stack, audited against the code.</h2>
          <p class="band-sub">Not a wrapper. Every capability below is a real subcommand with tests behind it.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="pillars">
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">train</span>
            <p>Pretrain, SFT, DPO / SimPO / KTO / ORPO, distillation, ES. Full PEFT bundle — LoRA, LoRA+, DoRA, VeRA, LoftQ, AdaLoRA, PISSA. WSD schedules, spike recovery, z-loss.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">eval</span>
            <p>BFCL, τ-bench, lm-eval (MLX adapter), HumanEval + sandbox, SQL execution, router, MILU, MTEB. Frozen baselines, slice metrics, exit-non-zero gates.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">serve</span>
            <p>OpenAI- and Ollama-compatible on one socket. Agent loop, tool dispatch, FSM-constrained JSON, persistent KV cache, speculative decoding, optional cloud escalation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">package</span>
            <p>Export to MLX, safetensors, CoreML. Quantize (GGUF / AWQ / GPTQ / HQQ), prune, merge, bake-LoRA — DoRA magnitudes included. Specialist model cards.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">inspect</span>
            <p>SAE features, ROME, MEMIT, tuned / logit lens, activation patching, linear probes, attention heatmaps. Know <em>where</em> the model decides, not just what it answers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-i mono-label">browser</span>
            <p>The same model trains in a browser tab via hand-written WebGPU kernels — Memory64, FlashAttention-2, blocked matmul. A from-scratch learning track, honest negative results and all.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= EXPERIMENTS ================= -->
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
        <header class="band-head">
          <h2>The work shows its scars.</h2>
          <p class="band-sub">
            A factory is a loop, not a demo. Failed runs become the next recipe — and
            all of it is written down, with the decision it forced.
          </p>
        </header>
        <ol class="ledger" role="list">
          <li>
            <span class="led-date mono-label">07-04</span>
            <div>
              <p class="led-what"><strong>Ref-free SimPO collapsed the SQL policy.</strong> Execution 0.860 → 0.080, degenerate fence-spam.</p>
              <p class="led-dec">→ <span class="tag">retry-training</span> preference tuning needs a reference anchor.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="led-date mono-label">07-11</span>
            <div>
              <p class="led-what"><strong>Reference-anchored DPO fixed the collapse.</strong> Execution recovered to 0.900, then 0.920 at higher pressure — no regression.</p>
              <p class="led-dec">→ <span class="tag">retry-data</span> execution was never the problem; the <code>Answer:</code> wrapper is a base-model prior.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="led-date mono-label">now</span>
            <div>
              <p class="led-what"><strong>Diagnosis corrected in the open.</strong> The 108 SFT targets were already bare SQL — so hygiene needs a generation-strength fix, not more DPO.</p>
              <p class="led-dec">→ next: constrained SELECT-prefix decoding.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <a class="band-more" href="/docs/attempt-ledger">The full attempt ledger →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= LEARN ================= -->
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <header class="band-head">
          <h2>Built to be learned from.</h2>
          <p class="band-sub">A ground-up curriculum and per-technique explainers — each tied to the paper it cites and the file where it lives.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="learn-grid">
          <a class="learn-card learn-lead" href="/docs/learn/curriculum">
            <span class="mono-label">the curriculum</span>
            <h3>Ground-up, in 10 modules</h3>
            <p>From <code>y = mx + b</code> to a self-improving factory. Every subsystem in the repo maps to an anchor in the coverage map — nothing is a black box.</p>
            <span class="learn-go">Start module 1 →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="learn-card" href="/docs/learn/tool-calling-frontier-parity">
            <span class="mono-label">case study</span>
            <h4>Frontier-parity at 4B</h4>
            <p>The headline result, the recipe, the honest tradeoffs.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="learn-card" href="/docs/interpretability">
            <span class="mono-label">interpretability</span>
            <h4>Where the model decides</h4>
            <p>Logit / tuned lens, patching, SAE, ROME, MEMIT.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="learn-card" href="/docs/distillation">
            <span class="mono-label">distillation</span>
            <h4>Teacher → student</h4>
            <p>KL + NLL mix, temperature, α, rejection sampling.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="learn-card" href="/leaderboard">
            <span class="mono-label">evals</span>
            <h4>The leaderboard</h4>
            <p>Drop a JSONL; compare by step, model, task.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= HONEST + RUN ================= -->
    <section class="band band-close">
      <div class="wrap honest-wrap">
        <div class="honest-col">
          <h2>Honest scope.</h2>
          <ul class="honest-list is">
            <li>A single-developer project, shipping in public, MIT.</li>
            <li>Mac-first — M-series, unified memory, MLX-Swift.</li>
            <li>A factory for <em>specialists</em>, not a general assistant.</li>
            <li>An OpenAI-compatible runtime any client already speaks.</li>
          </ul>
          <ul class="honest-list isnt">
            <li>Not a proven ship loop yet — the missing proof is a run that decides <strong>ship</strong>.</li>
            <li>Not multi-GPU or distributed. One device, one Mac.</li>
            <li>Not a cloud product. Nothing leaves the laptop unless you ask.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="run-col" data-theme="instrument">
          <span class="mono-label">run it</span>
          <pre class="run-block"><code><span class="c">// one Mac, from source</span>
git clone posttrainllm && cd native-mac
swift build --product posttrainllm

<span class="c">// train a specialist, gate it, serve it</span>
posttrainllm distill --teacher qwen3 --student ...
posttrainllm eval-gate --spec sql.json --candidate ...
posttrainllm serve --port 8080  <span class="c">// OpenAI-compatible</span></code></pre>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/quickstart">Full quickstart →</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="wrap foot-wrap">
      <span>posttrainllm — an LLM factory for one Mac. MIT.</span>
      <span class="foot-links">
        <a href="/artifacts">specialists</a>
        <a href="/docs/attempt-ledger">experiments</a>
        <a href="/docs/README">docs</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/sarthak-fleet/posttrainllm" rel="noopener">github ↗</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Default>

<style is:global>
  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  .landing { padding-bottom: var(--s-9); }
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(var(--s-8), 9vw, var(--s-10)); padding-bottom: var(--s-9); }
  .hero-kicker { margin-bottom: var(--s-5); }
  .hero-h1 { font-size: var(--step-5); font-weight: 640; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .hero-h1 .ox { color: var(--brand); }
  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 60ch; margin-top: var(--s-5);
    font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--fg-soft);
  }
  .hero-lede em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; font-weight: 560; }
  .hero-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-3); margin-top: var(--s-6); }

  /* factory-loop specimen (dark instrument card in the light page) */
  .loop {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--r-4);
    padding: clamp(var(--s-5), 3vw, var(--s-7));
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-3);
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .loop::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(120% 80% at 85% -10%, var(--live-wash), transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .loop-cap {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s-3); margin-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }
  .loop-live { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--live); }
  .loop-live .dot {
    width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--live-bright);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 var(--live-bright); animation: pulse 2.4s var(--ease-out) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes pulse {
    0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(72,229,194,0.5); }
    70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px rgba(72,229,194,0); }
    100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(72,229,194,0); }
  }
  .loop-steps {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--r-2); overflow: hidden;
  }
  .loop-steps li {
    padding: var(--s-4) var(--s-4) var(--s-5);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
    position: relative;
  }
  .loop-steps li:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .loop-steps li::after {
    content: "→"; position: absolute; right: -8px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%);
    color: var(--ink-55); font-size: 13px; z-index: 1; background: var(--paper-raised);
    width: 16px; text-align: center;
  }
  .loop-steps li:last-child::after { content: ""; }
  .ls-n { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-55); }
  .ls-k { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--fg-soft); font-weight: 500; }
  .loop-steps code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink); }
  .loop-steps code.ok { color: var(--live); }
  .loop-steps .ls-decide code { color: var(--brand); }
  .loop-note { margin-top: var(--s-5); font-size: var(--step-0); color: var(--fg-soft); max-width: 70ch; }
  .loop-note code { color: var(--live); font-size: 0.92em; }
  .loop-note .ship { color: var(--brand); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .loop-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .loop-steps li:nth-child(2n)::after { content: ""; }
    .loop-steps li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  }

  .hero-stats {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--s-8) 0 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: var(--s-6);
  }
  .hero-stats b {
    display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 620; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .hero-stats span { display: block; margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--fg-quiet); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .hero-stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }

  /* ---------- bands ---------- */
  .band { padding: var(--s-9) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .band-alt { background: var(--sunken); }
  .band-close { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-top: 0; }
  .band-head { max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: var(--s-7); }
  .band-head h2 { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
  .band-sub { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--fg-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .band-more { display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--s-6); font-weight: 550; color: var(--brand); }
  .band-more:hover { color: var(--brand-bright); }

  /* ---------- specialists ---------- */
  .spec-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: var(--s-5); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .spec-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .spec {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-3);
    padding: clamp(var(--s-5), 3vw, var(--s-7)); display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
    transition: box-shadow var(--dur-2) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur-2) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-2) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .spec:hover { box-shadow: var(--shadow-2); transform: translateY(-2px); border-color: var(--line-strong); }
  .spec-lead { border-top: 3px solid var(--brand); }
  .spec-top { margin-bottom: var(--s-4); }
  .spec-top .mono-label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--s-3); color: var(--live); }
  .spec-lead .spec-top .mono-label { color: var(--brand); }
  .spec-body { color: var(--fg-soft); margin-bottom: var(--s-5); }
  .spec-body strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 620; }
  .spec-body em { font-style: normal; color: var(--brand); font-weight: 560; }
  .spec-metrics { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-5); margin: 0 0 var(--s-5); padding-top: var(--s-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .spec-metrics div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
  .spec-metrics dt { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--fg-quiet); }
  .spec-metrics dd { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step-0); color: var(--fg); }
  .spec-metrics dd b { color: var(--live); font-weight: 600; }
  .spec-metrics dd.down { color: var(--brand); }
  .spec-link { margin-top: auto; font-weight: 550; color: var(--ink); }
  .spec-link:hover { color: var(--brand); }

  /* ---------- metric row ---------- */
  .metric-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: var(--s-4); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .metric-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .metric-row > div { padding: var(--s-5) 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .metric-row b { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--step-4); font-weight: 620; letter-spacing: -0.03em; display: block; }
  .metric-row .mu { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--live); display: block; margin-top: 2px; }
  .metric-row small { display: block; margin-top: var(--s-3); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--fg-quiet); }

  /* ---------- pillars ---------- */
  .pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--s-6) var(--s-7); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .pillars { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .pillar { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); padding-top: var(--s-4); }
  .pillar-i { display: block; color: var(--brand); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: var(--s-3); font-size: var(--step-0); letter-spacing: 0; }
  .pillar p { color: var(--fg-soft); font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .pillar em { font-style: normal; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 560; }

  /* ---------- ledger ---------- */
  .ledger { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .ledger li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr; gap: var(--s-5); padding: var(--s-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ledger li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .led-date { padding-top: 3px; color: var(--live); }
  .led-what { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.45; }
  .led-what strong { font-weight: 620; }
